step 1 : typescript install karne se pahle package.json setup karte h.
npm init -y

step 2 : install typeScript
npm i -D typescript

step 3.1 (optional) : agar aap global typescript install karte ho to aap tsc command directly use kar sakte ho,
lekin tsconfig.json tab bhi manually init karni padti hai

npm install -g typescript

step 3.2 : chahe TypeScript global ho ya local, tsconfig.json hamesha manually init karni padti hai.
local install me hum npx tsc --init use karte hain

npx tsc --init

ab aapne package.json file me jakar script :
"dev": "npx tsc",
"start": "node dist/index.js"

ab aapne tsconfig.json file me jana h niche diya hua file Layout agar comment h to comment remove karna h:
      // File Layout
    "rootDir": "./src",
    "outDir": "./dist",


most Recommended : aap local project me hi typescript ko install kate na ki global, global me Version controlnhi mil pata Team safe nhi hoti

ab etna karne ke bad  run kaise karte hai ?

1. npm run dev

Ye kaam karta hai: tsconfig.json read karta hai, Saare .ts files compile karta hai, Output JavaScript bana deta hai (usually dist/ folder me)

2. npm start 

👉 Ye compiled JS file ko run karta hai:
⚠️ Important:
Node TypeScript nahi samajhta, sirf JS samajhta hai
Isliye pehle dev run karna zaroori hai

Check version:
npx tsc --version

Q3: Kya npm run dev aur npm run start ek sath chala sakte hain?

Step 1️⃣ Install
npm i -D concurrently nodemon

Step 2️⃣ package.json
"scripts": {
  "dev": "concurrently \"tsc --watch\" \"nodemon dist/index.js\""
}

Step 3️⃣ Run
npm run dev

🔥 Bas ek command
🔥 Auto compile + auto restart
👉 Industry me yahi use hota hai

