typeScript + node :
aapne jo upar dekha vo sirf typescript + nodejs setup tha jo ki manually karna padta hai jab ham 
locally project me typescript install karte hai ab ho ye rha hai ki
aap ko ek entery point banana padta h kyu ki ye node js ka rule hai na ki typescript ka aur entry poin sir ek hi file ho sakti h
hame entry point ka name kuch bhi de sakte src folder ke andar like index.ts app.ts, main.ts, server.ts but
industry me index.ts sabse jyada prefferd kiya jata hai. agar entry file src/index.ts hai to uska compiled output dist/index.js banta hai
 yahi se .ts file .js file me compile hota hai agar error rahega to vo run se pahle show 
kar dega phir eske bad npm run start karte hai jisse hamare project ka output aata hai
Har file index.ts se directly attach nahi hoti, Import chain / layered architecture use hota hai h project me jitni bhi file hoti hai

next.js + typescript :
but jab ham next.js + typescript ke sath kam karte hai aur next.js ke sath sath typescript ko install karte hai
tab typescript ke related jitna bhi configration hota hai vo sab automatically nextjs karta hai
hame next.js me entery point ke liye agal se index.ts file nhi banani padti Next.js ke paas hidden entry files hoti hain.

Final clarity (notes ke liye) : 
✔️ Next.js me entry point hidden hota hai
✔️ Har page .tsx ek logical route hota hai
✔️ TypeScript automatically setup hota hai
✔️ tsc sirf type-check ke liye
✔️ SWC actual compiler hota hai
✔️ Developer ko entry file manage nahi karni


